course: dictionary
lesson: 1577
title: A charmer who wins people over
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A charmer is a person who is very pleasant and attractive, and who makes people like them easily. Read the words around the word to check. If the sentence says people warm to someone quickly, the word probably means a likeable person.
explain: Stories often use charmer for a smooth talker. A charmer can be kind, but sometimes they use their charm to get what they want. Ask yourself: does the charm seem honest, or is it a trick? The clues in the sentence will help you decide.
explain: The word also names a person who charms animals, such as a «snake charmer». In that case, the clues are about music, a pipe, or a snake swaying. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
fact: A charmer is a person who is very pleasant and attractive, and makes people like them easily.
fact: «A real charmer» is often said about a baby or a puppy that people cannot help loving.
fact: A charmer can also be a person who charms animals, such as a «snake charmer».
fact: Some charmers use their charm to get what they want, so a charmer is not always honest.
fact: Check the clues: if the sentence is about a pipe, music, or a snake, the word means the animal meaning.
exercise: «The puppy wagged its tail and everyone wanted to cuddle him. He is a real charmer.» What does charmer mean here? | A person who is always angry | A snake that dances to music | *Someone pleasant who makes people like them easily | A type of cake
exercise: «In the market, a snake charmer played his pipe while the snake swayed.» What is a snake charmer? | A zookeeper who feeds reptiles | A snake that sings to people | A shopkeeper who sells snakes | *A person who seems to make a snake move to music
exercise: Mum says, «Ellie is such a charmer, she always gets extra pudding!» What does Mum mean? | Ellie is a snake | Ellie is very tired | Ellie is always cross and never gets pudding | *Ellie is pleasant and wins people over to get what she wants
test: «Her smile was so warm that everyone at the party wanted to talk to her. She was a real charmer.» What does charmer mean? | A person who is always tired | A large bird that lives in trees | A person who hides from others | *A person who wins people over easily
test: Which phrase names a person who charms snakes? | snake tail | snake cage | *snake charmer | snake bite
exam: «The charmer smiled at the shopkeeper, then quietly took the watch.» What does charmer suggest here? | A helpful nurse at a hospital | A shy person who never speaks | *A pleasant person who uses their charm to get what they want | A snake that dances to music
